The communication line from the Service Room to the U.S. office basically runs through cable trays from the IT room to the ceiling of this office. After reaching the office ceiling, the connection from above to the wired communication outlets (or telephone/computer outlets) in the walls typically follows a pathway called EMT (galvanized steel conduit). The standards for this pathway, rough-in, and Power Distribution to supply power to them are all set by Dixie or EITIA, as will be discussed later.

For our electrical discipline, our scope includes the following major items:  
1. Providing power supply;  
2. Installing wiring or cable trays below;  
3. Ensuring proper Grounding and bonding.

